 rounding bug on a new branch. CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Its docstring and `tests/test_money.py` both expect banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`), so 2.665 rounded to 2.67 when the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the import and the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit 08d3cd5986).\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nThe advisory lookup didn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix relies on the test and the docstring, which both specify banker's rounding.\n\nMerging needs code-owner approval, so I haven't merged it.", "type": "text"}]}]}